//@version=6
// Demonstrates the two ways piner's book and pinelive's book silently diverge.
//
// The fixed quantity here (0.01 BTC) is a valid multiple of the instrument's
// quantity step (0.001), but 04-paper-sub-minimum.json declares a much larger
// `minOrderQty` (0.05). So on every entry:
//
//   piner   : books a long 0.01 position and starts accruing P&L on it
//   pinelive: target 0.01, actual 0, delta 0.01, snapped quantity 0.01
//             -> below minOrderQty -> returns action "noop", submits nothing
//             -> writes an `evaluation.completed` row and records a breaker
//                SUCCESS, even though the mirrored position never moved
//
// Then when the strategy closes, the second divergence appears: piner books a
// closed trade with a realized P&L, while pinelive computes target 0 against an
// actual of 0, sees a zero delta, and no-ops again. The strategy's entire trade
// lifecycle happens with zero broker activity, and nothing in the ledger says
// the two books disagreed.
//
// Position mirroring makes this safe (it can never sell a position you do not
// hold, because the actual is re-read from the broker before every plan) but it
// does not make it visible.
strategy("Sub-minimum quantity (silent divergence)",
     overlay = true,
     initial_capital = 10000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value = 0.01,
     process_orders_on_close = true)

fastLength = input.int(10, "fast", minval = 1)
slowLength = input.int(30, "slow", minval = 2)

fast = ta.sma(close, fastLength)
slow = ta.sma(close, slowLength)

if ta.crossover(fast, slow)
    strategy.entry("long", strategy.long)
if ta.crossunder(fast, slow)
    strategy.close("long")

plot(fast, "fast", color = color.teal)
plot(slow, "slow", color = color.orange)
